{
"dur": 61.899,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 7.2,
"text": "Over the next fifteen years, Americans moved trillions of dollars into index funds. A big share of it went to BlackRock.",
"end": 7.475
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 7.475,
"vo_start": 7.75,
"vo_end": 11.736,
"text": "By 2026, iShares alone held more than six trillion dollars.",
"end": 12.011
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 12.011,
"vo_start": 12.286,
"vo_end": 19.886,
"text": "Each fee is tiny. But a tiny fee on trillions of dollars, running automatically every day, is an enormous business.",
"end": 20.161
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 20.161,
"vo_start": 20.436,
"vo_end": 26.396,
"text": "And here's the part that matters. Every dollar that goes into an index fund buys a slice of every company in the index.",
"end": 26.671
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 26.671,
"vo_start": 26.946,
"vo_end": 36.184,
"text": "That's how BlackRock ends up holding around seven to eight percent of Nvidia, Microsoft and Apple. Nobody at BlackRock chose those stocks. The index did.",
"end": 36.459
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 36.459,
"vo_start": 36.734,
"vo_end": 43.253,
"text": "It isn't alone. Two other giants, Vanguard and State Street, grew the same way. Together they're called the Big Three.",
"end": 43.528
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 43.528,
"vo_start": 43.803,
"vo_end": 52.856,
"text": "Researchers at the University of Amsterdam found that, taken together, the Big Three were the largest shareholder in about nine out of ten companies in the S&P 500.",
"end": 53.131
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 53.131,
"vo_start": 53.406,
"vo_end": 60.949,
"text": "And shareholders get votes. On who sits on company boards, on how executives are paid, on big strategy questions.",
"end": 61.899
}
],
